## 🔍 Understanding On-Chart Visuals

| Visual Element | Color / Appearance | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| **C2 Label** | Neutral text at swing | Confirmed sweep candle swing extreme. |
| **xC2 Label** | Bright Red | Setup invalidated — price breached C2 extreme after CISD. |
| **Sweep Line** | Solid line across wicks | Price level where C1 liquidity was swept. |
| **CISD Line** | Blue (Bull) / Red (Bear) | Institutional Change in State of Delivery level. |
| **IC-CISD Dot (`●`)** | Blue / Red (Turns Gray) | Protected swing structure point. Turns gray once taken. |
| **T-Spot Box** | Shaded Rectangle | High-probability entry zone (HTF Open + EQ + CISD 50%). |
| **C3 (★ SMT)** | Purple Label | Ultra high-probability confluence: SMT active at entry zone. |
| **xC4 Label** | Bright Red | C4 continuation failed (breached C3 extreme). |
| **Dotted Level** | Horizontal dotted line | Untaken formation liquidity target. |
| **Projections** | Labeled deviation levels | Institutional standard deviation expansion targets. |

